{
  "description": "Golden keyboard-chord contract, shared by Android (KeyChordEncoder.kt), iOS (KeyChordEncoder.swift) and web (web/src/protocol/keyChord.ts). 'encode' pins the chord-to-PTY-bytes matrix: bytes_hex is the full lowercase-hex byte sequence, summary is the picker preview string, uses_csi_u drives the 'may not work in every CLI' hint, and same_as_plain_key discloses a chord that collapses onto an unmodified special's byte (Ctrl+I = Tab). 'parse_cases' pins the token grammar (modifiers accepted in any order, re-emitted as ctrl,alt,shift) and 'parse_rejected'/'encode_rejected' pin what must be refused so stale or forward-incompatible persisted tokens are dropped silently.",
